From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar grows with the screen as the title bars do

sg-shell's looks size the title bars by the screen: Style\Scale8, its
height in eighths of 800 px (1080p 11, 1200p 12), since David found them
"kinda small on a 1080p screen" (2026-10-02). The taskbar stayed 40 px
and its icons, text, Start, search box, clock, pager and Task View glyph
the same whatever the screen -- small beside the windows. Every size of
the bar now goes through that scale (SG_PX): its height on every edge and
in every look, its buttons, icons (the notification area's too), the
font of its labels and clock, the search box, Start, the clock's room;
read at start and again when a look sets the sizes
(SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS), so it follows at once. At scale 8 nothing
changes.

Test: test/barscale-gate.sh with test/barscale-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_BAR_NO_SCALE).
